e terrorists and other organised crime or something. basically enough to hit """100 points of id²""". we\'ve subsequently had massive data breaches of local telecommunication companies, most famously the 2022 optus 1. plus the authorities and governments can gain access to our persomal info really easily if they have our phone numbers.¹our medicare is somewhat different. it\'s 100% federal government run and owned, but it\'s definitely moreso universal healthcare than a kind of semi-insurance. there\'s still shit that isn\'t covered that should be (dental for adults, most mental health, lots of medical scans that aren\'t x-rays or ultrasounds...... it\'s fucked)²each piece of pii falls into a category that has different points. this checklist from the australian federal police (afp) is probably used the most. https://www.afp.gov.au/sites/default/files/PDF/NPC-100PointChecklist-18042019.pdf#Privacy #InfoSec #OpSec #FCC #Anonymity #Phones #Protest #uspol #auspol', 'publication_date': 'Sat, 25 Jul 2026 01:23:08 +0000', 'source': 'https://aus.social/@industrial_cream/116977834403750605', 'source_type': "['']", 'source_level': 2, 'text': [], 'observables': {'email-addr': ['industrial_cream@aus.social']}}, {'title': 'ChonkyChicken Steals Browser Credentials and Conducts Victim  SurveillanceChonkyChicken is a modular Windows remote access trojan built for credential theft and long term surveillance. It can hijack active browser sessions and explore internal networks.Pulse ID: 6a63fbea209182be9a2d07d8 Pulse Link: https://otx.alienvault.com/pulse/6a63fbea209182be9a2d07d8  Pulse Author: cryptocti Created: 2026-07-24 23:57:30Be advised, this data is unverified and should be considered preliminary. Always do further verification.#Browser #CyberSecurity #InfoSec #OTX #OpenThreatExchange #RemoteAccessTrojan #Trojan #Windows #bot #cryptocti', 'publication_date': 'Sat, 25 Jul 2026 00:22:57 +0000', 'source': 'https://social.raytec.co/@techbot/116977679860244168', 'source_type': "['']", 'source_level': 2, 'text': [], 'observables': {'domain-name': ['otx.alienvault.com'], 'email-addr': ['techbot@social.raytec.co']}}, {'title': 'CVE-2026-61884 (CRITICAL, CVSS 9.8) in Tycon TPDIN-Monitor-WEB2 v2.3.9: Server-side auth validation missing — empty creds grant admin access. Restrict management interface, monitor for unauthorized logins. https://radar.offseq.com/threat/cve-2026-61884-cwe-288-in-tycon-systems-tpdin-monitor-web2-38fd252c1e4f018a #OffSeq #CVE #IoT #Infosec', 'publication_date': 'Sat, 25 Jul 2026 00:22:57 +0000', 'source': 'https://infosec.exchange/@offseq/116977673191813338', 'source_type': "['']", 'source_level': 2, 'text': [], 'observables': {'domain-name': ['radar.offseq.com'], 'vulnerability': ['CVE-2026-61884']}}, {'title': 'Plexfiltration update: the AI work zone compliance tool has started emailing me thousands of pictures from a (I think) Saudi industrial facility again, to my internaluser.com domain. #infosec', 'publication_date': 'Sat, 25 Jul 2026 00:22:57 +0000', 'source': 'https://infosec.exchange/@SecureOwl/116977537011938688', 'source_type': "['']", 'source_level': 2, 'text': [], 'observables': {'domain-name': ['internaluser.com']}}, {'title': 'CVE-2026-66374 - Knot Resolver Heap-Based Buffer Overflow Remote Code Execution', 'publication_date': 'Sat, 25 Jul 2026 01:16:26 +0000', 'source': 'https://cvefeed.io/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-66374', 'source_type': "['']", 'source_level': 2, 'text': ['The following products are affected byCVE-2026-66374vulnerability. Even ifcvefeed.iois aware of the exact versions of the products that are affected, the information is not represented in the table below.', 'Common Attack Pattern Enumeration and Classification (CAPEC) stores attack patterns, which are descriptions of the common attributes and approaches employed by adversaries to exploit theCVE-2026-66374weaknesses.', 'We scan GitHub repositories to detect new proof-of-concept exploits. Following list is a collection of public exploits and pr